# Hostname allowlist for the egress proxy - POSIX extended regexes, one per
# line, matched (case-insensitively) against the request's host.
#
# EMPTY BY DEFAULT ON PURPOSE. With FilterDefaultDeny Yes in tinyproxy.conf,
# a file with no patterns denies everything, which is the whole point of the
# default `no-internet` mode. Adding a line here is a deliberate act.
#
# Anchor your patterns. `docs.ditto.live` unanchored also matches
# `docs.ditto.live.attacker.example`, because it is a substring match.
#
# To let the agent read the Ditto docs and nothing else:
#
#   ^docs\.ditto\.live$
#
# Remember what an allowlisted host actually is: a full-bandwidth, bidirectional
# channel to that host. It is a smaller door, not a one-way window.
